# CONFLICT — liability cap with Amendment No. 1 (ACME-NW-MSA-2026)

> Module Conflict_liability_cap_with_amendment
> Using Legal_types as T

This module is **expected not to execute** for claims on or after 2026-09-01. SYN-003 § 5.1
(Order Form No. 1) caps ordinary liability at 300% of the $240,000 annual fees, and
SYN-004 § 2.1 (Amendment No. 1) replaces MSA § 9.2 with a flat $500,000 for all claims.
Ordinarily MSA § 14.3 would let the Order Form win, but the Amendment switches that off:

  SYN-004 § 3.2 — This Amendment and any Order Form issued under the MSA are of equal rank.
  Neither this Amendment nor any Order Form shall be deemed to take precedence over the
  other, and Section 14.3 of the MSA shall not apply as between this Amendment and any
  Order Form.

So there is no exception to declare, and the two definitions collide. Compare
`liability_cap_acme_northwind.catala_en`, which is the same cap resolved by § 14.3 because
no amendment disclaims it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope AmendedLiabilityCap:
  input annual_fees content money
  input claim_type content T.ClaimType
  input claim_date content date

  output cap content money
```

## SYN-003 § 5.1 — the Order Form's general cap

  Notwithstanding Section 9.2 of the MSA, each party's aggregate liability arising out of
  or related to the Services ordered under this Order Form shall not exceed three hundred
  percent (300%) of the Annual Fees stated above.

```catala
scope AmendedLiabilityCap:
  definition cap
    under condition
      claim_date >= |2026-07-01| and claim_type = T.ClaimType.Ordinary
    consequence equals annual_fees * 3.0
```

## SYN-004 § 2.1 — the Amendment's flat cap

  Section 9.2 of the MSA is deleted and replaced with the following: "Each party's
  aggregate liability arising out of or related to this Agreement, and to any Order Form
  issued under it, shall not exceed five hundred thousand dollars ($500,000) for all
  claims of every kind."

```catala
scope AmendedLiabilityCap:
  definition cap
    under condition claim_date >= |2026-09-01|
    consequence equals $500,000
```
